# =============================================================================
# Horse Brand · environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need.
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# In Vercel, add each PUBLIC_* variable in:
#   Project Settings → Environment Variables → All Environments
# Astro exposes only variables prefixed with PUBLIC_ to client code; everything
# else stays server-only.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudinary (image CDN)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public cloud name. Appears in every image URL, so it's safe to expose.
# If unset, the codebase falls back to the value hardcoded in
# `src/lib/cloudinary.ts`. No API key / secret is required because the site
# only consumes public delivery URLs (no uploads, no signed URLs).
PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD=dukv3ov6t

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future: newsletter backend
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Currently the footer form just logs to console. When you wire a real
# provider (Mailchimp, Brevo, Tiendanube newsletter, etc.), add its endpoint
# here and consume it in `src/components/sections/Footer.astro`.
# NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=https://api.example.com/subscribe
# NEWSLETTER_API_KEY=your-secret-key
